To find each value of $\maroonD y$, we need to take each value of $\greenD x$ and $\goldE{\text{subtract } \dfrac{1}{4}} $.

For example, when $\greenD {x} = \greenD{\dfrac{1}{4}}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{y} &= \greenD{\dfrac{1}{4}} \goldE{-\dfrac{1}{4}} \\\\
\maroonD{y} &= \maroonD{0}
\end{align}$
